                <pb facs="0897" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg797"/>

                <head>No. 507.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Mathews.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-04-13"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 13,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 165.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 353, transmitting a copy
                    of the circular of the Moorish minister of foreign affairs relative to the
                    Sultan’s desire that Moorish subjects naturalized in foreign countries shall
                    become amenable to Moorish jurisdiction, has been received, and I take pleasure
                    in informing you that your action thereunder, based upon the treaty of September
                    16, 1836, between the governments of the United States of America and Morocco,
                    meets with entire approval.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
